/math-academy-id "q-54628" :question/problem "If $6{q}^{2}+2=0$, then $q=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{q}^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ 6{q}^{2} & =-2 \\\\ {q}^{2} & =-\\frac{2}{6} \\\\ {q}^{2} & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nq=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{1}{3}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $q$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068707 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "701015d7-cc6a-52ff-b40d-627a640cd0fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d75c601-096a-5903-b04a-0034749e71d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555173} {:answer/id #uuid "908fc347-0be1-50c0-99cd-da5164897e6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555339} {:answer/id #uuid "982355ec-96f1-512b-a246-51b13af7a290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555365} {:answer/id #uuid "d76312f5-0e57-5076-954e-87ce4299933b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 